# Paths that Template sync must not carry from the blueprint into this repo.
# gitignore syntax. Everything listed here is repo-specific; everything left out
# is a convention the template owns and may overwrite.
#
# This file is never synced itself: the action keeps the downstream copy and
# reverts template changes to it. Edit it here, per repo.

# Names and describes THIS project; the template's copy describes the template
# and its bootstrap command.
README.md

# The project's own orientation doc, written per repo by /domain-modeling.
CONTEXT.md

# Decisions of this project. The template ships the ADR format, not the records.
docs/adr/

# Written against this codebase; the template has no architecture to index.
docs/architecture/

# Per-repo ignores and attributes accumulate (build output, tooling, local
# scratch). A sync that overwrote them would break the working tree.
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Path-scoped rules cite this repo's files. The template's copies point at paths
# that do not exist here, and citations that cannot resolve are exactly what the
# doc guards fail on.
.claude/rules/

# Not a convention: the template's own issue/PR templates and CODEOWNERS are
# about maintaining the blueprint.
.github/CODEOWNERS
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
